---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Safe Sport & Child Protection Standards | NAA Regina, SK"
  description="Mandated Saskatchewan safeguards, Sask Sport framework compliance, Respect in Sport certification, CRC-VSS screening, and CAC Rule of Two at National Athletics Academy in Regina."
>
  <Header />

  <!-- Page Hero -->
  <section class="page-hero" aria-labelledby="safety-hero-heading">
    <div class="container-naa" style="position:relative;z-index:1;text-align:center;">
      <div class="animate-fade-up">
        <span class="badge" style="background:rgba(221,170,64,0.2);color:var(--color-naa-gold);margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
          Saskatchewan Sport Framework Compliance
        </span>
        <h1 id="safety-hero-heading" style="font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3.5rem);color:white;margin-bottom:1rem;">
          Safety &amp; Standards
        </h1>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);font-size:1.15rem;max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.7;">
          At National Athletics Academy, participant safety is our highest operating standard. We adhere strictly to the safeguards recommended by Sask Sport, the Coaching Association of Canada, and sport safety frameworks.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 Mandated Safeguards Pillars -->
  <section class="section-padding" aria-labelledby="safeguards-heading">
    <div class="container-naa">
      <div class="reveal" style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:4rem;">
        <span class="badge" style="background:rgba(131,22,27,0.1);color:var(--color-naa-maroon);margin-bottom:1rem;">Parent Trust Center</span>
        <h2 id="safeguards-heading" class="gold-accent-center" style="font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3.5vw,2.75rem);margin-bottom:1rem;">
          The Three Non-Negotiable Safeguards
        </h2>
        <p style="color:#4b5563;font-size:1.05rem;max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.7;">
          Every child in Regina deserves a secure, encouraging, and abuse-free sporting environment. NAA enforces these three core safety protocols without exception:
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="naa-grid-3">
        <!-- Pillar 1: Respect in Sport -->
        <div class="card reveal" style="padding:2.5rem 2rem;border-top:5px solid var(--color-naa-navy);display:flex;flex-direction:column;height:100%;">
          <div style="width:60px;height:60px;border-radius:16px;background:rgba(2,31,71,0.08);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:var(--color-naa-navy);margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
            <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="badge" style="background:rgba(2,31,71,0.08);color:var(--color-naa-navy);align-self:flex-start;margin-bottom:1rem;">
            Required for All NAA Coaches &amp; Activity Leaders
          </span>
          <h3 style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--color-naa-navy);margin-bottom:1rem;">Respect in Sport (Activity Leader)</h3>
          <p style="color:#374151;font-size:0.92rem;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.5rem;flex:1;">
            In Saskatchewan, youth sports operate under the <strong>Sask Sport Respect in Sport (RiS) framework</strong>. Required for all NAA coaches and activity leaders, 100% of NAA coaches, assistant coaches, and administrative personnel must hold active Respect in Sport Activity Leader certification prior to stepping onto the court or field.
          </p>
          <div style="background:var(--color-naa-grey);border-radius:10px;padding:1rem;font-size:0.82rem;color:#4b5563;">
            <strong style="color:var(--color-naa-navy);display:block;margin-bottom:0.25rem;">What this covers:</strong>
            Bullying prevention, harassment identification, discrimination safeguards, and emotional athlete well-being.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Pillar 2: Screening -->
        <div class="card reveal" style="padding:2.5rem 2rem;border-top:5px solid var(--color-naa-maroon);display:flex;flex-direction:column;height:100%;animation-delay:0.1s;">
          <div style="width:60px;height:60px;border-radius:16px;background:rgba(131,22,27,0.08);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:var(--color-naa-maroon);margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
            <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"/></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="badge" style="background:rgba(131,22,27,0.08);color:var(--color-naa-maroon);align-self:flex-start;margin-bottom:1rem;">
            Vulnerable Sector Screened
          </span>
          <h3 style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--color-naa-maroon);margin-bottom:1rem;">CRC-VSS Police Checks</h3>
          <p style="color:#374151;font-size:0.92rem;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.5rem;flex:1;">
            All coaches, instructors, and volunteers working with youth participants undergo thorough <strong>Criminal Record Checks with Vulnerable Sector Screening (CRC-VSS)</strong> through the Regina Police Service or local RCMP detachments.
          </p>
          <div style="background:var(--color-naa-grey);border-radius:10px;padding:1rem;font-size:0.82rem;color:#4b5563;">
            <strong style="color:var(--color-naa-maroon);display:block;margin-bottom:0.25rem;">Renewal Cycle:</strong>
            Screenings are renewed on strict multi-year cycles, with mandatory annual statutory declarations of no changes.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Pillar 3: Rule of Two -->
        <div class="card reveal" style="padding:2.5rem 2rem;border-top:5px solid var(--color-naa-gold);display:flex;flex-direction:column;height:100%;animation-delay:0.2s;">
          <div style="width:60px;height:60px;border-radius:16px;background:rgba(221,170,64,0.15);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:#926508;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
            <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="badge" style="background:rgba(221,170,64,0.18);color:#926508;align-self:flex-start;margin-bottom:1rem;">
            CAC Mandate
          </span>
          <h3 style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--color-naa-navy);margin-bottom:1rem;">CAC Rule of Two</h3>
          <p style="color:#374151;font-size:0.92rem;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.5rem;flex:1;">
            NAA follows the <strong>Coaching Association of Canada (CAC) Rule of Two</strong>: interactions between coaches and participants always take place in open, observable settings with two screened adults present, never one-on-one behind closed doors.
          </p>
          <div style="background:var(--color-naa-grey);border-radius:10px;padding:1rem;font-size:0.82rem;color:#4b5563;">
            <strong style="color:var(--color-naa-navy);display:block;margin-bottom:0.25rem;">Core Standard:</strong>
            Two screened adults are always present or interactions occur in open, observable settings.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Physical Safety & Concussion Protocols -->
  <section class="section-padding" style="background:var(--color-naa-navy);color:white;" aria-labelledby="physical-safety-heading">
    <div class="container-naa">
      <div class="naa-grid-2" style="align-items:center;">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="badge" style="background:rgba(221,170,64,0.2);color:var(--color-naa-gold);margin-bottom:1rem;">Physical Wellbeing</span>
          <h2 id="physical-safety-heading" style="font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3.5vw,2.5rem);color:white;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
            Concussion Protocols &amp; Emergency Action Plans
          </h2>
          <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
            Sport should build resilience, not risk. NAA maintains rigorous on-site health standards across all gymnasium, turf, and martial arts facilities in Regina:
          </p>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.25rem;">
            <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;">
              <div style="width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:8px;background:rgba(221,170,64,0.15);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:var(--color-naa-gold);font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0;">1</div>
              <div>
                <h3 style="font-size:0.98rem;color:var(--color-naa-gold);margin-bottom:0.25rem;font-family:var(--font-outfit);">Sask Sport Concussion Recognition</h3>
                <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);line-height:1.6;">Follows Parachute Canada &amp; Sask Sport Concussion Protocol. When in doubt, the athlete sits out — mandatory physician clearance required before Return-to-Play.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;">
              <div style="width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:8px;background:rgba(221,170,64,0.15);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:var(--color-naa-gold);font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0;">2</div>
              <div>
                <h3 style="font-size:0.98rem;color:var(--color-naa-gold);margin-bottom:0.25rem;font-family:var(--font-outfit);">First Aid &amp; CPR Certified Staff</h3>
                <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);line-height:1.6;">Every active training block has a designated First Aid / CPR certified lead coach with fully inspected first-aid kits on site.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;">
              <div style="width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:8px;background:rgba(221,170,64,0.15);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:var(--color-naa-gold);font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0;">3</div>
              <div>
                <h3 style="font-size:0.98rem;color:var(--color-naa-gold);margin-bottom:0.25rem;font-family:var(--font-outfit);">Venue Emergency Action Plans (EAP)</h3>
                <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);line-height:1.6;">Specific emergency procedures, AED locations, and emergency contacts documented for each Regina school and fieldhouse venue.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- MMA Assurance -->
        <div class="reveal" style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.05);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12);border-radius:24px;padding:2.5rem;">
          <div style="width:48px;height:48px;border-radius:12px;background:rgba(221,170,64,0.15);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:var(--color-naa-gold);margin-bottom:1rem;">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"></path></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 style="font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--color-naa-gold);margin-bottom:1rem;font-family:var(--font-outfit);font-weight:800;">
            Special Safeguards in MMA Fundamentals
          </h3>
          <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);font-size:0.92rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
            NAA offers MMA fundamentals (striking, grappling, self-defence) strictly as <strong>skill development, discipline, and fitness</strong> — never unsanctioned fighting.
          </p>
          <ul style="list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.75rem;font-size:0.88rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);">
            <li style="display:flex;gap:0.6rem;align-items:center;">
              <span style="color:var(--color-naa-gold);">✓</span> No head strikes permitted in youth cohorts (Ages 4–12)
            </li>
            <li style="display:flex;gap:0.6rem;align-items:center;">
              <span style="color:var(--color-naa-gold);">✓</span> Mandatory protective gear (shin guards, headgear, mouthguards) for any youth sparring
            </li>
            <li style="display:flex;gap:0.6rem;align-items:center;">
              <span style="color:var(--color-naa-gold);">✓</span> Strict 1:8 coach-to-athlete supervision on all mat training
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- CTA -->
  <section style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--color-naa-maroon) 0%,var(--color-naa-maple) 100%);padding:4rem 0;">
    <div class="container-naa" style="text-align:center;">
      <div class="reveal">
        <h2 style="font-size:2rem;color:white;margin-bottom:1rem;">Experience the NAA Standard</h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:520px;margin:0 auto 2rem;line-height:1.7;">
          Explore our structured multi-sport programs backed by certified Saskatchewan coaching and safety compliance.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <a href="/programs/" class="btn btn-gold btn-lg">Explore Programs</a>
          <a href="/registration/" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg">Register Your Athlete</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
